{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1447952-time-in-between-descents","id":1447952,"title":"Time in between Descents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-08T10:43:57-07:00","id":1447952,"title":"Time in between Descents","content":"Did the 2nd edition say anything about how often a Cult can wake up a Mummy. Looking at the descent drop chart, it looks like Mummies spend about 2 weeks being very powerful, then a few months being less powerful, and as they get to Sekhem 1 or 2, they can spend several months but are fairly weak. Is there a hard and fast rule as to how long must transpire between a Mummy dying, and their cult trying to wake them up again with their Sekhem reset to 10?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T13:24:30-07:00","id":1447976,"title":"","content":"Second Edition says it won't be available for one story, which according to the chart for making Descent rolls is estimated at a little under 20 weeks. I personally vastly prefer first editions rules (in pretty much every respect, actually, but to be specific...) of 7 weeks as a baseline, plus 2-20 weeks determined by two dice, minus the level of the relic. So at the least the relic ceases to function for 8 weeks, at most it will remain out of commission for half a year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T15:30:33-07:00","id":1447991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1447952-time-in-between-descents?p=1447976#post1447976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second Edition says it won't be available for one story, which according to the chart for making Descent rolls is estimated at a little under 20 weeks. I personally vastly prefer first editions rules<b> (in pretty much every respect, actually, but to be specific...)</b> of 7 weeks as a baseline, plus 2-20 weeks determined by two dice, minus the level of the relic. So at the least the relic ceases to function for 8 weeks, at most it will remain out of commission for half a year.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">No edition warring, please.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T22:17:42-07:00","id":1448021,"title":"","content":"So speaking as a guy who has been posting on one incarnation of these forums or another for years now, is there some kind of guide for what opinions are to no longer be expressed around here? It would be extremely helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T07:17:39-07:00","id":1449652,"title":"","content":"I did some reading and I think I was able to answer my question. In theory, a cult should be able to awaken a mummy constantly so long as they have relics tied to the lifeweb of the tomb that the mummy. In theory, the mummy should be able to do it's descent, and when it is finished, the cult can use relics to begin another descent, rinse and repeat...<br /> <br /> In practice, this would probably not be so simple.<br /> <br /> When a mummy goes into a death cycle they are expected to surrender relics to their Judge. Not doing so will make the Judge angry and one does not want to make a Judge angry. In second edition, the Judges can sent Avatars which are very powerful which can either make the life of a mummy very miserable, or just suck up Sekhem from an environment, potentially draining any relics in a region (including relics in the tomb of the Mummy). <br /> <br /> Furthermore, when a Mummy dies and faces her judge, she must pass through a number of Trials, if she does poorly (such as not giving up Relics I would imagine), her next descent will be nasty and have some flawed conditions.<br /> <br /> Plus...having a relic in her tomb is like a big target. Other Arisen will want to seek them out to surrender to their Judges, or simply to drain them. In addition, bane mummies and Amkhata will be seeking them out and that is a great deal of unwanted attention.<br /> <br /> Finally, the mummy herself might want to drain it to complete a mission. If you need just one more reset before dropping in power, that temptation might be too great. <br /> <br /> That is my understanding of why descents don't happen more often. Usually cultists need to find relics that are not part of the lifeweb and are useless after a Call so the frequency is more limited outside of a Sothic turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}